  "SubGoals": [],
  "Description": "This Goal, named Stop, is designed to terminate a debug session. It first checks if debugging is active; if not, it returns without making any changes. If debugging is active, it sends a stop command to the debug channel, sets the debug status to inactive, and closes the communication connection. Additionally, if a terminal process is still running, it will be killed, and a JavaScript command is executed to indicate that the debugger has been terminated.",
  "Visibility": 1,
  "GoalFileName": "Stop.goal",
